{
	"_doc": "Two fixture sets the test expands into the CANARY_FIXTURES layout. A head is a short name the test hashes to 40 hex. A comment is `r:<head>` (a factory/pr-review round on that head, posted by factory), `hold` (a ROUND LIMIT notice, posted by sf-reed) or `note` (any other comment). `status` maps a head to its factory/pr-review state. `open` is the repo record's open_pr_counter. The bad set breaks every gate; its recreate-reopen replacement gets a round after the inherited hold, its concurrent-events PR's only round is on a stale head, and its same-head-no-progress PR has two rounds on two heads.",
